
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:redraw@

%9Description:%9

    Redraws the whole screen. This is useful when the display got garbled,
    for example by output written to the terminal by another program.

    The same is done by the refresh_screen key, bound to Ctrl-L by default.

%9Examples:%9

    /REDRAW

%9See also:%9 BIND, RESIZE, SCROLLBACK

